<BaseLayout title="About | UXO.INFO" description="About UXO.INFO and its approach to public-interest information.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">About the project</p><h1>Information before noise.</h1><p class="lead">UXO.INFO is an independent, evolving public-interest information project about unexploded ordnance and the consequences it can leave behind.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><h2>A practical starting point.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>We are building a resource for people who need a reliable introduction, a better path to sources, or a place to begin a serious conversation about UXO.</p><p>The project is English-first for now. It is being designed so that further languages, regional research, maps, and documented local context can be added when they are ready to be useful—not simply present.</p><p>UXO.INFO is not a clearance operator, emergency service, or substitute for official safety direction.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section--quiet"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Method</p><h2>Specific about what we know.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>We aim to distinguish sourced material, general context, and future ambitions. When a claim needs a source, the source should be visible. When information is incomplete, it should not be dressed up as certainty.</p><p>Corrections, primary material, local expertise, and responsible collaboration are welcome.</p><a class="action-link" href="/contact">Contact the project</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
